Description: Set SCAN_OFFSET to 8 (Debian #538859)

  The original SCAN_OFFSET of 9 skips one byte too far into a Common Log
  Format line before locating the date substring, which can shift the
  parsed date and mis-order merged log streams. Debian tracked this as
  bug #538859 (2009) and shipped the offset-8 fix in every release since.

Upstream: https://bugs.debian.org/538859
Origin: https://sources.debian.org/src/mergelog/4.5.1-10/debian/patches/fix-SCAN_OFFSET.patch

--- a/src/mergelog.c
+++ b/src/mergelog.c
@@ -34,3 +34,3 @@
 #define DATE_SIZE 14
-#define SCAN_OFFSET 9
+#define SCAN_OFFSET 8
 #define SCAN_SIZE 512
